Ladybird resets inherited styles on the root of native media controls.
The root inherits visibility, pointer-events, and cursor from the host.
WebKit resets its media-controls-container and inherits all three.
Blink styles its current-time and time-remaining displays directly, and
Gecko sets a system font on the positionDurationBox around its labels.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all showed elapsed
time inside a parent with zero line height, before metadata had loaded.
With zero line height, wide spacing, centered text, and uppercase
on the audio element, Chrome and WebKit painted the same controls as on
an unstyled element. Firefox painted them differently. All three hid the
controls and excluded them from hit testing on a hidden host.

Ladybird keeps the native audio and video controls left-to-right when
an ancestor sets its direction with HTML or CSS. Chrome 158.0.8127.37,
Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 kept Play on the left in both cases.
Blink sets the direction on its media controls pseudo-element, Gecko
on .videocontrols, and WebKit on .controls-bar.
